==Early entrants==
===College underclassmen===
This year saw a continued rise of collegiate underclassmen and other players of similar nature declaring entry into the NBA draft. This year initially saw a total of 47 eligible players enter the draft at first, but seven of these players (including [[Cory Carr]] from [[Texas Tech Red Raiders men's basketball|Texas Tech University]], former [[DePaul Blue Demons men's basketball|DePaul University]] player [[Ronnie Fields]] from the [[St. Paul Slam!]] in the [[International Basketball Association]], the [[Greeks|Greek]] born [[Dimitrios Papanikolaou]] of the [[Olympiacos B.C.|Olympiacos Piraeus B.C.]] in [[Greece]], Larell Redic from [[Utah State Aggies men's basketball|Utah State University]], Dawood Thomas from the [[California Vulcans|California University of Pennsylvania]], the [[Turkey|Turkish]]-[[FR Yugoslavia|Yugoslavia]]n born [[Mirsad Türkcan]] of the [[Anadolu Efes S.K.|Efes Pilsen]] in [[Turkey]], and the [[Argentina|Argentinian]]-[[Spain|Spanish]] born [[Lucas Victoriano]] of the [[Olimpia Basketball Club|Olimpia Venado Tuerto]] in [[Argentina]]) would later decline their entry for this year's draft. Including the likes of high school phenom [[Tracy McGrady]] from [[Mount Zion Christian Academy]], the [[Slovenia]]n born [[Marko Milič]] of the [[KK Olimpija|Smelt Olimpija]] in [[Slovenia]], and former [[Central Connecticut Blue Devils men's basketball|Central Connecticut State University]] player [[Keith Closs]] of the Norwich Neptunes from the Atlantic Basketball Association minor league, the number of qualified underclassmen would increase from 37 only in college to 40 total players. Regardless, the following [[college basketball]] players successfully applied for early draft entrance.<ref name=tdr>{{cite web |title=1997 Underclassmen |url=https://www.thedraftreview.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=3044:1997-underclassmen&catid=136&Itemid=384 |website=The Draft Review | date=August 4, 2007 |access-date=December 16, 2022}}</ref>

